spec ww10-crossing-writes-lpg: 2 sessions, 20 permutations
# WW10 through the lpg API. A refused write dooms the lpg transaction, so its commit
# returns the conflict and publishes nothing — where the Cypher arm reports the
# poisoned transaction instead. The verdict (nothing of a refused transaction
# survives) is the same; the error each surface reports at COMMIT differs.

starting permutation: s1a s1b2 s1c s2b2 s2a s2c
step s1a: lpg: SetNodeProperty(A, v, 1)
step s1b2: lpg: SetNodeProperty(B, v, 1)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s2b2: lpg: SetNodeProperty(B, v, 2)
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2a: lpg: SetNodeProperty(A, v, 2)
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
ERROR: serialization conflict
final final: MATCH (n:Item) RETURN n.name AS name, n.v AS v ORDER BY name
name|v
----+-
"A" |1
"B" |1
(2 rows)

